'''History/Origins'''

Originally referred to a block of carved wood matching the size and shape of a customer’s head that was used to build a wig or hat. According to the OED, the first literary reference using the word as a derogatory term dates to 1549. Additionally: 

“No man but a blockhead ever wrote, except for money.” - Samuel Johnson (1791)
As quoted in James Boswell (1791) ''The Life of Samuel Johnson''